Subject: [SUMMARY] HP LaserJet 4M+ printing
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076339121635


	
	I have received many replies to my request for info about HP
	LaserJet 4M+ printing. The basic problem is that if two jobs are queued
	back-to-back (but not on the same command line) the second one
	is frequently lost. The printer is used on an ethernet network using
	TCP/IP protocol.

	Solutions:
	(1)Commercial products. THIS IS NOT AN ENDORSEMENT, IT IS FYI YOU
	SHOULD RESEARCH THESE COMPANIES IF INTERESTED. Emulex apparently makes
	a substitute for the HP JetDirect card called NetJet. Cost is about
	US$400. I was contacted directly by a company called Open Systems
	Management which sells software management tools under the marketing
	name COSMOS. Another user suggested that the appletalk interface on
	the JetDirect is quite robust and installing cap(?) and the packet
	filter kernel module would allow appletalk spooling. The guy I talked
	to at DEC said another user had no trouble with a card made by NCD.

	(2)Another kind soul has will be sending his personal software solution.	He is quite busy at this time, however when he follows up I'll see if
	I can get it working here. Perhaps this may be distributed later with
	the author's permission.

	As an aside, one person reported that things worked fine until the
	3.2-->4.0 upgrade, at which point the problem occurred. People on
	other platforms (Sun and HP (obviously I guess)) reported that things
	worked OK. 

	I also had trouble with parallel interface printing. I apologize for not	checking the archives for this one. Remove the "rw" line from 
	printcap and it goes. More on this later.	-pat

