Thanks again for the responses!
     
VT420 DB25 pinout:
     
Pin  2 - TXD
Pin  3 - RXD
Pin  4 - RTS
Pin  5 - CTS
Pin  6 - DSR
Pin  7 - SGND (Signal Ground)
Pin  8 - RLSD (Carrier Detect)
Pin 12 - SPDI (Speed Indicator)
Pin 20 - DTR
Pin 23 - Speed Select
     
VT420 MMJ pinout:
     
1 - DTR
2 - TXD+ ("Held in mark state (-) when characters are
not being sent. In modem control modes, sends data only when DSR and DTR signals
are on.")
3 - TXD- ("Provides the common ground reference potential 
for transmitted signals TXD+ and DTR")
4 - RXD- ("Provides the common ground reference potential 
for received signals RXD+ and DSR)
5 - RXD+
6 - DSR
     
6 being on the offset key side.
     
Here's how the signals go through a H8585 with a H8571 (8 pin MMJ to 6 pin)
     
signal DS90M  H8584 (MMJ)     signal H8571  (RS232) 
.             (RJ45)                 (MMJ)
RXD GND 1       1     4        DTR     1     20 
RXD     2       2     5        TX+     2     2 
TXD GND 3       3     3        TX-     3     7 
.       4       4     6        RX-     4     7 
.       5       5     *        RX+     5     3 
TXD     6       6     2        DSR     6     8
DTR     7       7     1                  4 tied to 5 
DSR     8       8     6                  6 tied to 8
     
"The information comes from pages 4-109, 4-107 of the Fall 93 OPEN DECconnect 
Applications Guide (EC-G2570-42), and the DECserver 90M owners manual, page A-5.
(* means not connected)"
     
Bob
     
